<title>GERMANY: BOBSLEIGH-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>BOBSLEIGH-EUROPEAN CHAMPIONSHIP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>KOENIGSSEE, Germany 1997-01-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of two-man</p>
<p>event at European bobsleigh championships on Saturday:</p>
<p> 1. Italy I (Guenther Huber/Antonio Tartaglia)	 one minute</p>
<p>36.45 seconds (48.17/48.28 seconds).</p>
<p> 2. Germany I (Sepp Dostthaler/Thomas Platzer)	 1:36.46</p>
<p>(48.19/48.27).</p>
<p> 3. Switzerland I (Reto Goetschi/Guido Acklin)	 1:36.68</p>
<p>(48.35/48.33).</p>
<p> 4. United States II (Brian Shimer/Robert Olesen)    1:37.08</p>
<p>(48.34/48.74).</p>
<p> 5. Switzerland III (Christian Reich/Donat Acklin)   1:37.16</p>
<p>(48.59/48.57).</p>
<p> 6. Germany III (Matthias Benesch/Lars Bolte)	  1:37.17</p>
<p>(48.59/48.58).</p>
<p>7. United States III (Tuffield Latour/Darin Steele) 1:37.24</p>
<p>(48.57/48.67).</p>
<p> 8. Germany II (Rene Spies/Christoph Heyder)	   1:37.32</p>
<p>(48.59/48.73).</p>
<p>World Cup standings after five events:</p>
<p> 1. Italy I   164 points.</p>
<p>2. Canada I  152.</p>
<p>3. Germany I 140.</p>
